Z||000000||86se/lambo||12-13-2000||12:40 AM||||when i got the car back from being stretched<BR>i noticed the radiator fan will not come on.<BR>with the fan switch grounded there is power to the relay and to one of the spade connectors at the fan. My 86 2.8 has the 6 lead relay...that the hanes manual says is for the 4 cyl. with a 2 speed fan... so thats kinda wierd. asper diagram there should be a ground strap off the fan. I bought a new fan motor..wont work.. and it did not have a ground strap...any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||12-13-2000||05:02 PM||||I recall seeing a ground wire that runs along the plastic frame of the fan and connects to the chassis with one of the mounting bolts.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||William Federle||12-13-2000||05:08 PM||||One of the two wires from the fan motor goes to a screw that bolts the square fan assembly to the frame. I think it has a star-washer to bite into the frame.<BR>||||reg||1
